-- v0.11 economy recalibration (owner, Oct 14): "prices are too cheap, so moving around doesn't create a
-- real sink or tension. Recalibrate prices against the ability to earn so there's always a need to make
-- more money."
--
-- What was wrong: a shift pays C$120 for 25 Energy and a home-cooked meal gives 25 Energy for about C$5,
-- with no limit on shifts, so every extra shift netted about C$115 and daily costs (C$4 to 95) barely
-- registered. Now:
--   * A work day is at most 3 shifts (shiftsPerDay), across every job. do_action enforces it.
--   * Everyday costs are about 2.3 times higher: meals, visits, events, the bar, groceries, the subway and
--     taxis. Clout per dollar comes down to match (0.6 to 0.25), so visits give about the same clout.
--   * The birth lottery is C$5,000 to 10,000 (was 3,000 to 6,000), so even the lowest roll still covers
--     a first week in any home (the v0.8 rule).
--   * Weekly bills: rent C$1,750 / C$2,600 / C$4,500 (was 600 / 900 / 1,600), the phone C$60 (was 25).
--     Rent is read from these settings when it's billed, so every player moves to the new rent.
--   * Gigs pay less (side 2 to 3 shifts, pro 5 to 6, big 10 to 12) and daily tasks pay C$25 to 50 with a
--     C$100 bonus, so a full day earns about C$900 before gigs.
--   * The Shop: fashion and makeup about 2.2 times, luxury 2.5 times, cars and houses 1.5 times (car
--     rental too). Car insurance stays 0.5% of the car's price a week.
-- A full day (3 shifts, the tasks, a side gig) earns about C$900; a modest day (studio rent, meals,
-- travel, one night out) costs about C$530, so saving for anything in the Shop takes days to months.

